*> Implementation test (lane 002-lane-mobsb3, T8100; docs/protocol/17 section 4.9a, 49 section 2.4): the status effect store of mobs (core/src/mob-effects.cob).
*> Add and replacement rules, level and ticks, periodic poison, wither and regeneration with the interval rule, expiry, removal, instant effects with the undead inversion,
*> and the clearing of a removed entity.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-MOB-EFFECTS.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY MOBEFFECT.
 01 WS-PLAYER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-ENTITY-ROW          PIC X(66).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TYPE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW2                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ID2                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-YAW                 FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 01 WS-EFFECT              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-AMP                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DUR                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FLAGS               BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
 01 WS-LEVEL               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TICKS               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-GOT                 BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "MS-TEST-OPEN" USING WS-PLAYER
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "minecraft:cow" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-TYPE WS-ENTITY-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE PL-X(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-X
     MOVE PL-Y(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-Y
     MOVE PL-Z(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-Z
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING PL-DIM(WS-PLAYER) WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-ROW
     MOVE EN-ID(WS-ROW) TO WS-ID
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING PL-DIM(WS-PLAYER) WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-ROW2
     MOVE EN-ID(WS-ROW2) TO WS-ID2

*>   Add and level.
     MOVE 18 TO WS-EFFECT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-AMP
     MOVE 100 TO WS-DUR
     CALL "MEF-ADD" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-AMP WS-DUR WS-FLAGS
     CALL "MEF-LEVEL" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-LEVEL WS-TICKS
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a a mob effect has level amplifier + 1" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-LEVEL TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a a mob effect keeps its ticks" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 100 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-TICKS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Another entity does not have it.
     CALL "MEF-LEVEL" USING WS-ID2 WS-EFFECT WS-LEVEL WS-TICKS
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a effects belong to one entity" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-LEVEL TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   A weaker amplifier is ignored, a longer one with the same amplifier replaces, a stronger one replaces.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-AMP
     MOVE 500 TO WS-DUR
     CALL "MEF-ADD" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-AMP WS-DUR WS-FLAGS
     CALL "MEF-LEVEL" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-LEVEL WS-TICKS
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a a weaker amplifier does not replace" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2100 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = WS-LEVEL * 1000 + WS-TICKS
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-AMP
     MOVE 300 TO WS-DUR
     CALL "MEF-ADD" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-AMP WS-DUR WS-FLAGS
     CALL "MEF-LEVEL" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-LEVEL WS-TICKS
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a the same amplifier with more ticks replaces" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2300 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = WS-LEVEL * 1000 + WS-TICKS
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 3 TO WS-AMP
     MOVE 10 TO WS-DUR
     CALL "MEF-ADD" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-AMP WS-DUR WS-FLAGS
     CALL "MEF-LEVEL" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-LEVEL WS-TICKS
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a a stronger amplifier replaces" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 4010 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = WS-LEVEL * 1000 + WS-TICKS
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "MEF-REMOVE" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT
     CALL "MEF-LEVEL" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-LEVEL WS-TICKS
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a a removed effect is gone" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-LEVEL TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Poison I for 100 ticks fires at d 100, 75, 50, 25: 4 damage on a cow of 10 health.
     MOVE 10 TO EN-HEALTH(WS-ROW)
     MOVE 0 TO WS-AMP
     MOVE 100 TO WS-DUR
     CALL "MEF-ADD" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-AMP WS-DUR WS-FLAGS
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 100
         MOVE 0 TO EN-HURT(WS-ROW)
         CALL "MEF-TICK" USING WS-ROW
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a poison I for 100 ticks hurts 4 times" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 6 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-HEALTH(WS-ROW) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "MEF-LEVEL" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-LEVEL WS-TICKS
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a the effect expires after its duration" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-LEVEL TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Poison never kills.
     MOVE 1 TO EN-HEALTH(WS-ROW)
     MOVE 200 TO WS-DUR
     CALL "MEF-ADD" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-AMP WS-DUR WS-FLAGS
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 100
         MOVE 0 TO EN-HURT(WS-ROW)
         CALL "MEF-TICK" USING WS-ROW
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a poison does not hurt at health 1" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-HEALTH(WS-ROW) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "MEF-CLEAR" USING WS-ID
*>   Regeneration I for 100 ticks fires at d 100 and 50: heals 2, never above the maximum.
     MOVE 9 TO WS-EFFECT
     MOVE 5 TO EN-HEALTH(WS-ROW)
     MOVE 100 TO WS-DUR
     CALL "MEF-ADD" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-AMP WS-DUR WS-FLAGS
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 100
         CALL "MEF-TICK" USING WS-ROW
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a regeneration I for 100 ticks heals 2" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 7 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-HEALTH(WS-ROW) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 10 TO EN-HEALTH(WS-ROW)
     CALL "MEF-ADD" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-AMP WS-DUR WS-FLAGS
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 100
         CALL "MEF-TICK" USING WS-ROW
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a regeneration stops at the maximum health" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 10 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-HEALTH(WS-ROW) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Wither I for 100 ticks fires at d 80 and 40: 2 damage.
     MOVE 19 TO WS-EFFECT
     MOVE 10 TO EN-HEALTH(WS-ROW)
     CALL "MEF-ADD" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-AMP WS-DUR WS-FLAGS
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 100
         MOVE 0 TO EN-HURT(WS-ROW)
         CALL "MEF-TICK" USING WS-ROW
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a wither I for 100 ticks hurts twice" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 8 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-HEALTH(WS-ROW) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   An infinite effect never expires.
     MOVE 1 TO WS-EFFECT
     MOVE -1 TO WS-DUR
     CALL "MEF-ADD" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-AMP WS-DUR WS-FLAGS
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 50
         CALL "MEF-TICK" USING WS-ROW
     END-PERFORM
     CALL "MEF-LEVEL" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-LEVEL WS-TICKS
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a an infinite effect stays" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-LEVEL TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Instant health heals 4 << a, instant damage hurts 6 << a.
     MOVE 3 TO EN-HEALTH(WS-ROW)
     MOVE 5 TO WS-EFFECT
     CALL "MEF-INSTANT" USING WS-ROW WS-EFFECT WS-AMP
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a instant health I heals 4" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 7 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-HEALTH(WS-ROW) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO EN-HURT(WS-ROW)
     MOVE 6 TO WS-EFFECT
     CALL "MEF-INSTANT" USING WS-ROW WS-EFFECT WS-AMP
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a instant damage I hurts 6" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-HEALTH(WS-ROW) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   The entity removal clears the effects.
     CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-ROW
     CALL "MEF-LEVEL" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-LEVEL WS-TICKS
     MOVE 1 TO WS-EFFECT
     CALL "MEF-LEVEL" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-LEVEL WS-TICKS
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a a removed entity keeps no effect" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-LEVEL TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   A full table takes no more entries.
     MOVE 3 TO WS-EFFECT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-AMP
     MOVE 50 TO WS-DUR
     MOVE 0 TO WS-GOT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > ME-MAX + 1
         COMPUTE WS-ID = 90000 + WS-I
         CALL "MEF-ADD" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-AMP WS-DUR WS-FLAGS
         CALL "MEF-LEVEL" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-LEVEL WS-TICKS
         ADD WS-LEVEL TO WS-GOT
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance US14 17§4.9a a full effect table takes no more" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE ME-MAX TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-GOT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   An out of range effect id is ignored.
     MOVE 40 TO WS-EFFECT
     MOVE 90001 TO WS-ID
     CALL "MEF-ADD" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-AMP WS-DUR WS-FLAGS
     CALL "MEF-LEVEL" USING WS-ID WS-EFFECT WS-LEVEL WS-TICKS
     MOVE "acceptance US14 49§2.4 an effect id above 39 is ignored" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-LEVEL TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-MOB-EFFECTS.
 COPY CORETEST.
 COPY MOBSPTEST.
